// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ReichsmanInvuln 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P502714354" "Invulnerable Reichsman"
// DetailString :
"P753679711" "During the 5th Column invasion of Boomtown, you encountered Reichsman. He boasted of being superchanged and unstoppable, and he was. Nothing you did could touch him, and he took the Freedom Phalanx down with ease.<br><br>You need to find the source of Reichsman's power and counter it, to stop this 5th Column threat."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ComputerFiles 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2947354341" "Reichsman's Computer Files"
// DetailString :
"P2850484742" "These files are dossiers on various Marcus Coles from alternate Earths. It appears that Reichsman himself is a version of Marcus Cole from a world where the Germans won World War II!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ComputerFiles2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P400419146" "Reichsman's Plan"
// DetailString :
"P3837158937" "These files detail Reichsman's plans to make an alliance of equals with four powerful arch villains. With Reichsman at the head of this "Council of Villains," he would have all of the resources he needed to run rampant over Paragon City!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeOneClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2357723955" "Return of the Reichsman"
// DetailString :
"P1267977632" "It all started when you got a call from Dr. Kahn, a noted historian. He had word that some villains were trying to break into City Hall so they could pillage the Omega Team time capsule. You arrived just in time to find the villains in the process of the theft, but were unable to stop one of them from escaping through a portal with what they were after. You followed them and found yourself in an old 5th Column base. Troops were coming through some kind of strange portal, which you shut down, ending that threat -- for now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeTwoClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2410507050" "It all started when you got a call from Dr. Kahn, a noted historian. He had word that some villains were trying to break into City Hall so they could pillage the Omega Team time capsule. You arrived just in time to find the villains in the process of the theft, but were unable to stop one of them from escaping through a portal with what they were after. You followed them and found yourself in an old 5th Column base. Troops were coming through some kind of strange portal, which you shut down, ending that threat -- for now.<br><br>The 5th Column threat continued when you received word that they were invading Boomtown! You went there to help fight them off, defeating the 5 Generals who were directing the operation and shutting down the portals that were allowing the 5th Column to pour their forces into the streets of Boomtown. But your victory wasn't complete; your activities attracted the attention of a foe from history -- Reichsman! You don't know how he escaped from where he'd been incarcerated, but he was back and more powerful than you could have possibly imagined. You were forced to retreat from Boomtown and now must seek another way to defeat this arch foe."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeThreeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2410809586" "You responded to a break in at City Hall which lead you to a supposedly abandoned base that was actually alive with 5th Column activity. That was just foreshadowing for what came next: a 5th Column invasion of Boomtown! You responded to the invasion, defeating generals and shutting down troop portals. But then the arch-villain Reichsman showed up. He was supercharged and the closest thing to invincible you'd ever seen. You were forced to retreat so you could find a way to take him down.<br><br> Those investigations lead you back to a old 5th Column base under Boomtown. Once you had cleared the place of the 5th Column, you were able to search through the computer system, recovering a file that had information on Marcus Coles from alternate dimensions. It seemed that Reichsman himself was an alternate version of Statesman, and he was kidnapping his counterparts and some how using them to empower himself!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFourClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3095342497" "You responded to a break in at City Hall which lead you to a supposedly abandoned base that was actually alive with 5th Column activity. That was just foreshadowing for what came next: a 5th Column invasion of Boomtown! You responded to the invasion, defeating generals and shutting down troop portals. But then the arch-villain Reichsman showed up. He was supercharged and the closest thing to invincible you'd ever seen. You were forced to retreat so you could find a way to take him down.<br><br> Those investigations lead you back to a old 5th Column base under Boomtown. Once you had cleared the place of the 5th Column, you were able to search through the computer system, recovering a file that had information on Marcus Coles from alternate dimes ions. It seemed that Reichsman himself was an alternate version of Statesman, and he was kidnapping his counterparts and some how using them to empower himself!<br><br>You next consulted with Tina MacIntyre on the nature of Reichsman's dimensional empowerment. She suggested you might be able to 'ground' this power out if you had access to energy from his home world. So you used Portal Corps. technology to travel back to Axis Earth, where you tapped five energy sources to power a device that would dimensionally "ground" Reichsman with the energy from his home world. You plan to use that energy to neutralize Reichsman's advantage and take him down, once and for all."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL9_ReturnoftheReichsman_StrikeForce 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3509325330" "Reichman's Plans"
// tDetailString :
"P778368948" "These plans for conquest remind you of the time when you saved Paragon City from the 5th Column in an adventure you call<br><br>The Return of the Reichsman<br><br>When a break in at City Hall lead you to a base that was rife with 5th Column activity, you knew something big was up. Your hunch was proved right when the 5th Column invaded Boomtown, so you headed there to shut them down. Though you defeated their generals and shut down the troop portals, a super-charged Reichsman arrived forcing you to retreat and find some way to defeat him.<br><br>Your investigations lead you to a 5th Column base where you recovered information that revealed Reichsman was an alternate version of Statesman, and was collecting other alternate versions of himself from which he could steal power, making him practically invincible. Working on the theory you could somehow "ground" this power out with the proper energy source, you went to Axis Earth where you tapped 5 energy sources.<br><br>You returned to your home and traveled to the 5th Column Base in Boomtown to confront Reichsman, only to find him in conference with four of the most powerful arch-villains around! You shattered his plans of an alliance of evil and captured the arch-villains, but Reichsman managed to slip away in the end. Somehow, you don't think you've seen the last of him."

